 when we cross\nthe northern gates. move! we\nneed to open it somehow"},resp_outro={"the march sent forces to\ncrush us. we must march!"}},{id="soldado",x=600,y=208,spr1=52,spr2=53,nome="sol. gareth",morto=false,fala_inicial={"after long days in mirk,\nwe reach her threshold!\nthe princess is so close!","yet... the air tastes of\nash. what is thy intent,\nwarrior?"},opcoes1={"1. i must turn south.","2. is the path clear?"},resp_caminho={"clear? in this ruined land?\nnay. keep thy blade drawn."},fala_sul={"south? 'tis impossible!\nwe felled the bridge to halt\nthe enemy march behind us.","why seek those dead lands?\nwhat draws thee south?"},opcoes2={"1. glory and conquest.","2. to save lost souls."},resp_arrogante={"thy hubris will end thee.\nyet... find grove timber.\nstout wood spans the chasm."},resp_generoso={"a noble doom, warrior.\nseek timber in the grove.\nthou mayst bridge the void."}},{id="profeta",x=552,y=64,spr1=63,spr2=112,nome="prophet",morto=false,fala_inicial={"all that exists, exists for\na reason. what god sealed to\nguard the world, no man\nmust ever unseal.","wars fade into shadow, yet\nlight and dark battle on in\nevery breath we take.","yet the light shall return\nto its throne, even if its\nbearer must endure pain."},opcoes1={"1. dark skin, dark mind.","2. light will reign."},resp_pele={"shall it be so? do thoughts\nbelong to flesh, or does\nthe abyss speak in thee?","i studied long years in the\nwestern temple. god's truth\nshall reach every soul.","thou art privileged to walk\nthis path, dark knight."},resp_luz={"thou art wise. they say the\nlight was kept in the castle\nto be hidden away.","someday it shall reveal its\ntrue form. was it kept to be\nprotected from something?"},opcoes2={"1. captors took her.\n   i shall rescue her."},resp_resgate={"a bold claim...","yet... something is wrong\nwith thee. 'tis not light\ni see in thy shadow.","seek that light in the\nsouth by helping souls.\ni hope to see it soon."}},{id="barricada",x=432,y=80,spr1=68,spr2=68,nome="barricade",morto=false,fala_inicial={"behold, a sturdy barricade\nof hewn timber obstructeth\nthy path."},opcoes1={"1. smite it to ruin.","2. depart in peace."},resp_quebrar={"the timber yieldeth to thy\nmight.","thou hast gathered wood."},resp_sair={"thou leavest it unbroken."}},{id="barricada",x=432,y=88,spr1=68,spr2=68,nome="barricade",morto=false,fala_inicial={"behold, a sturdy barricade\nof hewn timber obstructeth\nthy path."},opcoes1={"1. smite it to ruin.","2. depart in peace."},resp_quebrar={"the timber yieldeth to thy\nmight.","thou hast gathered wood."},resp_sair={"thou leavest it unbroken."}},{id="soldado_caido",x=544,y=448,spr1=40,spr2=40,nome="fallen sol.",morto=false,fala_inimigos={"stay back... *cough*...","kill those beasts before\nthey finish me..."},fala_inicial={"do not approach... *sob*...","my blood is unworthy...\ni might corrupt thee..."},opcoes1={"1. what hath happened?","2. the castle is near."},resp_oq={"*he ignores thee*","no matter what ruin we\ncause... 'tis not enough.","the march of the north is\ntoo vast... they will\nslaughter us all.","they sealed the gates... \nsmashed the gears...\nthe general took the key.","the pain... 'tis too much...","turn back! 'tis impossible\nto save the princess...","we are doomed... doomed!"},resp_castelo={"the castle? *cough*","arcane magic sealed the\ngates tight...","they shattered the gears...\nno one shall pass...","the northern general...\nhe took the key.","the pain... 'tis too much...","turn back! 'tis impossible\nto save the princess...","we are doomed... doomed!"},opcoes2={"1. thou art unworthy."},resp_indigno={"please... ahhgh!"}},{id="ferreiro",x=240,y=48,spr1=113,spr2=114,nome="smith",morto=false,fala_inicial={"please, spare me!\nthe war hath already taken\neverything from me.","i pose no threat to thee.\ni am but an honest worker.\nmen in armor took my wife\nand daughter...","they took them only for the\ngolden color of their hair."},opcoes1={"1. fear not, i mean no harm.","2. obey me, or thou diest."},resp_humilde={"thank the heavens...\nhow may a humble smith\nserve a knight as thee?"},resp_desumilde={"*he trembles in fear*\ny-yes, my lord... whatever\nthou commandest, i shall do."},opcoes2={"1. forge a gear for the gate"},resp_engrenagem={"a gear for the castle gate?\nit is a mighty task, but yes\ni can forge it.","however, i lack materials.\ni need iron of the highest\nquality to withstand the\nweight of those doors.","bring me pure iron, and\ni shall craft thy mechanism."},resp_ferro={"...pure iron. truly.\ni believed thou wouldst not\nreturn. iron is near\nimpossible to find in these\ntimes of war.","but here it is. very well.\ni shall honor my word.\n*he works in silence,\nthe hammer ringing\nagainst the dark*","...done. take it, knight.\nthe gear for the castle\ngate. i pray it opens\nthe way to whatever thou\nseekest in those halls."}},{id="aldeao",x=936,y=112,spr1=105,spr2=106,nome="wounded man",morto=false,fala_inicial={"war never changeth...\nit matters not who claims\nthe crown. the poor always\npay in blood and ash."},opcoes1={"1. how to reach the castle?","2. what happened here?"},resp_castelo_aldeao={"the castle? the war took\neverything and all of us.\na curse guards those doors.\nnone may draw near."},resp_oque_aldeao={"the march swept over us.\nthe war took all we had.\nand the castle is cursed.\nnone may draw near."},opcoes2={"1. help me break the curse."},resp_ajuda={"help a soldier? never!\nmy wife and daughter\nsleep in the ruins.\nsoldiers bring only ruin."},opcoes3={"1. aid me, or thou diest.","2. aid me, and i depart."},resp_ameaca={"*he trembles in pain*\na legend saith the well to\nthe north grants wishes...","but only if it receives\ninnocent blood, corrupting\nlight with darkness.","that is all i know.\nnow leave! draw not the\nmarch upon us!"},resp_partida={"if thou wilt leave us...\na legend saith the well to\nthe north grants wishes...","but only if it receives\ninnocent blood, corrupting\nlight with darkness.","that is all i know.\nnow leave! draw not the\nmarch upon us!"}}}end function init_morte()morte_timer=0morte_fase=0char_index=0linhas_morte={"wherefore hast thou turned","from me, my child?","","sufficed not the dignity","of my gift?","","may thy memory be forgotten."}fragmentos={}end function update_morte()morte_timer+=1if morte_fase==0and morte_timer>60do morte_fase=1for e=1,20do add(fragmentos,{x=64,y=64,vx=(rnd(4)-2)*1.5,vy=(rnd(4)-3)*1.5,vida=60+rnd(40)})end morte_timer=0elseif morte_fase==1and morte_timer>100do morte_fase=2morte_timer=0elseif morte_fase==2do if morte_timer%3==0do char_index+=1end end for e in all(fragmentos)do e.x+=e.vx e.y+=e.vy e.vy+=.1e.vida-=1if e.vida<=0do del(fragmentos,e)end end end function draw_morte()camera()for e=1,30do pset(rnd(128),rnd(128),e%2==0and 9or 0)end if morte_fase==0do spr(60,60,60)elseif morte_fase==1or morte_fase==2do if morte_fase==1and morte_timer<10do spr(61,60,60)end for e in all(fragmentos)do pset(e.x,e.y,9)end end if morte_fase==2do local e,t=0,30for a in all(linhas_morte)do local n=#a local o=64-n*2if e+n<=char_index do print(a,o,t,6)e+=n else local i=char_index-e if i>0do local e=sub(a,1,i)print(e,o,t,6)end e+=n break end t+=10end end end function escrever_diario(e)add(meu_diario,e)notif_timer=120end function init_inventario()inv_aba=1pagina_diario=1meus_itens={}meu_diario={}end function update_inventario()if btnp(5)do estado="jogo"end if btnp(4)do inv_aba+=1if inv_aba>2do inv_aba=1end end if inv_aba==2do if btnp(0)and pagina_diario>1do pagina_diario-=1end if btnp(1)and pagina_diario<#meu_diario do pagina_diario+=1end end end function draw_inventario()rectfill(10,10,118,118,0)rect(10,10,118,118,7)if inv_aba==1do print("--- thy belongings ---",14,14,10)if#meus_itens==0do print("thy pouch remaineth empty.",14,30,5)else for e=1,#meus_itens do print("- "..meus_itens[e],14,20+e*10,7)end end elseif inv_aba==2do local e=#meu_diario if e==0do e=1end print("--- thy journal (leaf "..pagina_diario.."/"..e..") ---",14,14,9)if#meu_diario==0do print("thou hast not written yet.",14,30,5)else print(meu_diario[pagina_diario],14,30,7)end print("<- and -> to turneth leaf",14,100,5)end print("[z] switch  [x] returneth",14,110,6)end